Registers the clean-room platform-oidc relying-party module (D-01/D-02 of
Phase 26 plan 05) into AuthModule: Twenty's OSS codebase has no OIDC RP
extension point, and twenty-apps only renders inside the authenticated
workspace shell, so a pre-authentication OIDC Authorization Code + PKCE
handshake against the platform's own broker is structurally unreachable
through the custom-app extension framework — the same limitation that
already forced patch 0001. This is the second deliberate, documented core
edit. All real RP logic lives in new files under
packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/auth/platform-oidc/ (clean-room
AGPL code, no Enterprise-licensed Twenty file copied/derived/referenced); this
patch only registers PlatformOidcAuthController/PlatformOidcAuthService —
two import lines plus one entry each in the controllers/providers arrays.
See docs/twenty-fork-policy.md for the full policy record.

Apply from the twenty-fork/ root: git apply PATCHES/0002-platform-oidc-auth-module.patch

